          "id": 2288666946,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I don't know. On one hand, I think `size > 0` shows you intention better than `size != 0`. On the other end, if you have a bug (and it has happened to me), you will look at your code cluelessly, wondering why the code that should execute only if size is greater than 0 is executing also in case of negative numbers (forgetting that size is unsigned).\n\nBottom line, I will change them in a separate MR.",
