        {
          "id": 2289804671,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "> On one hand, I think `size > 0` shows you intention better than `size != 0`.\n\nThe intent is presumably \"only append data if we have data to append\"; there should never be a negative amount of data to append (meaning \"remove data from the packet\"?), a negative value would presumably be from a routine that returns a positive number for \"I got some data for you\", zero for \"there's no data\", and a negative number for \"something else happened, e.g. an error\".",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
